            <ArticleTitle>Visible-light-mediated oxidative demethylation of N6-methyl adenines.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>10734-10737</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7cc05544g</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report a simple protocol that affords oxidative demethylation of N6-methyl groups in N6-methyl adenines (m6A). The biologically compatible photocatalyst riboflavin prompts a highly selective C-H abstraction from N6-methyl in adenines under the irradiation of a visible blue LED light, affording a novel and highly selective biomimetic demethylation of m6A and related N-methyl adenine analogues.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
